# Shell scripts keep LF in the working copy, on every platform.
#
# The desk here is Windows with core.autocrlf=true, and harness/tsan.sh is meant
# to be run from that same checkout under WSL — ThreadSanitizer needs Linux. A
# CRLF checkout makes the shebang `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, which bash reports as
# "bad interpreter" with the carriage return invisible in the error. Without
# this line a fresh clone would ship a script that cannot run on the only
# platform it targets.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Replay traces are the project's ground truth and are compared byte for byte;
# nothing may rewrite their line endings on the way through a working copy.
*.ndjson -text
